# Component Architecture Standards - MANDATORY

## File Structure Requirements - EXACT

### Component Directory Structure
```
src/components/ComponentName/
  ├── ComponentName.tsx          # Main component file
  ├── ComponentName.module.css   # Component-specific styles
  ├── index.ts                   # Export barrel (optional)
  └── types.ts                   # Component-specific types (if needed)
```

### Page Structure
```
src/pages/
  ├── HomePage.tsx
  ├── AboutPage.tsx
  └── ContactPage.tsx
```

### Global Structure
```
src/
├── components/           # Reusable components
├── pages/               # Page components
├── hooks/               # Custom React hooks
├── utils/               # Utility functions
├── types/               # TypeScript type definitions
├── data/                # Static data and content
├── styles/              # Global styles only
└── assets/              # Images, icons, etc.
```

## Component Naming Conventions

### File Naming
- Components: `PascalCase.tsx` (e.g., `HeaderNavigation.tsx`)
- CSS Modules: `PascalCase.module.css` (e.g., `HeaderNavigation.module.css`)
- Utilities: `camelCase.ts` (e.g., `formatDate.ts`)
- Hooks: `camelCase.ts` starting with `use` (e.g., `useLocalStorage.ts`)

### Component Export Pattern
```typescript
// Component.tsx
import styles from './Component.module.css';

interface ComponentProps {
  title: string;
  children?: React.ReactNode;
}

const Component: React.FC<ComponentProps> = ({ title, children }) => {
  return (
    <div className={styles.container}>
      <h1 className={styles.title}>{title}</h1>
      {children}
    </div>
  );
};

export default Component;
```

